   "source": {
    "label": "thm:ucb",
    "number": "Theorem 4.1",
    "quote": "Given a stochastic bandit instance with known $T$, let $\\Delta_i = \\mu_* - \\mu_i$, and let $\\Delta = \\min_{i:\\Delta_i>0} \\Delta_i$. Then for any $T>0$, there exists an algorithm that uses $O(1)$ words of space and achieves regret O( \\sum_{i:\\Delta_i>0} \\frac{1}{\\Delta_i} \\log (\\Delta_i/\\Delta ) \\log T )."
   },
   "confidence": "high",
   "notes": "Paper's Delta is the minimum positive gap (Delta_min). Regret measured as pseudo-regret (max over arms of difference of expectations). Note log(Delta_i/Delta) is 0 for arms with Delta_i = Delta; the proof's bound includes additive log(1/delta)/Delta_i terms, so the statement is literally as written."
  },
